+# Cancellation
+
+For whoever changes pantry order cancellation or answers a member who cannot cancel in the app. Cancellation closes
+when packing starts, two hours before the pickup slot. Members had been cancelling after volunteers packed their
+bags, leaving fresh food to be thrown away; a banner asking them to cancel earlier had not stopped it.
+
+## Cutoff
+
+A member may cancel in the app only before the cutoff. At exactly two hours before the pickup slot, and after that,
+cancellation is refused. For a 17:00 pickup, cancellation is allowed before 15:00 and refused from 15:00 onward.
+The eligibility check is [`can_cancel`](../../larder/cancellation.py).
+
+The packing shift starts two hours before each slot: earlier cancellations cost no packed bag, while later ones
+do. By October 7, 25 bags of fresh food had been thrown away that month despite the banner. The
+[issue 31 discussion](../../notes/issue-31.md) records why the cutoff was introduced.
+
+## After the cutoff
+
+A member who cannot come calls the pantry, and volunteers decide what to do. The agreement in issue 31 requires the
+pantry's phone number in the refusal message.
+
+## Known limits
+
+The repository implements only the eligibility check; it contains neither a refusal message nor a pantry phone
+number, so the agreed message cannot be verified here. After the cutoff, use the phone fallback above; volunteer
+decisions are outside the eligibility check.
